# Normalise line endings on checkout, whatever OS clones this next.
#
# Shell scripts, Dockerfiles and nginx config are COPYied into Linux images and
# executed there. A CRLF checkout on Windows bakes a literal carriage return
# into the file, which breaks them in ways that look like something else
# entirely — a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang, or a redirect target written as
# "default.conf\r" that nginx's `*.conf` glob then silently fails to match, so
# nginx boots with zero server blocks and never listens on port 80.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.template  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
